  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a downward trend (e.g., dropping from ~85 to ~79), failing to account for volatility spikes.",
    "Forecast horizon is systematically over-optimistic; true outcomes consistently fall below model predictions by 10-20 points during the first 10 days of the forecast window.",
    "Sentiment history (values > 0.6) correlates with immediate price spikes in true outcomes, but the model fails to capture this momentum and instead predicts a slow, linear recovery.",
    "When sentiment is low or neutral (0.0-0.25), the model's linear projection ignores sudden mean-reversion events where prices drop sharply below the trend line.",
    "Model assumes smooth continuity; true outcomes show high-frequency volatility with sharp reversals that occur regardless of recent sentiment direction.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately 15-20 points to the first week of any 30-day forecast when the last 5 days of history are trending down."
  ]
}
